1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,710
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,774 --> 00:00:10,134
Which one lets only some light pass through?

3
00:00:11,214 --> 00:00:12,614
One, clear glass.

4
00:00:13,694 --> 00:00:15,254
Two, frosted glass.

5
00:00:16,334 --> 00:00:17,914
Three, a wooden door.

6
00:00:19,763 --> 00:00:21,273
Hold on to your answer!

7
00:00:24,095 --> 00:00:25,565
You against the Buddies!

8
00:00:25,825 --> 00:00:27,055
Lock in first.

9
00:00:27,325 --> 00:00:29,145
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:29,415 --> 00:00:32,035
A little goldfish is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:32,295 --> 00:00:33,525
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:34,101 --> 00:00:35,431
Today you'll learn:

13
00:00:35,628 --> 00:00:36,998
The torch test.

14
00:00:37,202 --> 00:00:38,272
Transparent.

15
00:00:38,607 --> 00:00:39,837
Translucent.

16
00:00:40,605 --> 00:00:41,545
Are you ready?

17
00:00:41,985 --> 00:00:42,755
Three!

18
00:00:43,135 --> 00:00:43,795
Two!

19
00:00:44,165 --> 00:00:44,815
One!

20
00:00:45,235 --> 00:00:45,955
Go!

21
00:00:46,459 --> 00:00:48,009
Here is our torch test.

22
00:00:48,279 --> 00:00:49,239
A torch.

23
00:00:49,509 --> 00:00:50,379
A sheet.

24
00:00:50,649 --> 00:00:52,329
A white card behind it.

25
00:00:52,542 --> 00:00:54,882
Never shine a torch at anyone's eyes.

26
00:00:55,546 --> 00:00:56,836
I am too big to hide.

27
00:00:56,996 --> 00:00:58,886
So my robot will hide for me!

28
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:01,364
Sheet one: clear glass.

29
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:02,754
Look closer.

30
00:01:03,406 --> 00:01:04,376
Torch on.

31
00:01:04,956 --> 00:01:08,106
The light goes into the glass, and out the other side.

32
00:01:08,469 --> 00:01:10,469
A bright spot lands on the card.

33
00:01:11,069 --> 00:01:12,919
Most of the light passed through.

34
00:01:16,226 --> 00:01:18,826
Now the robot stands behind the glass.

35
00:01:19,396 --> 00:01:20,916
We can see it clearly.

36
00:01:24,342 --> 00:01:26,092
I can see every button!

37
00:01:26,970 --> 00:01:28,440
Here are the book's words.

38
00:01:28,652 --> 00:01:29,952
Say it with me!

39
00:01:30,663 --> 00:01:33,463
Some materials allow most light to pass through them.

40
00:01:33,993 --> 00:01:36,023
These materials are transparent.

41
00:01:39,622 --> 00:01:43,572
You can clearly see objects placed behind transparent materials.

42
00:01:44,834 --> 00:01:46,244
Frosted glass next!

43
00:01:46,304 --> 00:01:48,384
I will push the torch right up close!

44
00:01:49,708 --> 00:01:51,268
Something is not right.

45
00:01:51,538 --> 00:01:53,718
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

46
00:01:53,998 --> 00:01:54,958
Hold on!

47
00:02:00,471 --> 00:02:01,601
Arms crossed?

48
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:03,031
One finger up!

49
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,531
The torch moved.

50
00:02:04,831 --> 00:02:08,191
In a good test, we change one thing only: the sheet.

51
00:02:08,762 --> 00:02:09,422
Oops!

52
00:02:09,552 --> 00:02:10,602
Same torch.

53
00:02:10,682 --> 00:02:11,752
Same place.

54
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,663
Round one: the question from last time!

55
00:02:15,943 --> 00:02:18,303
Which one lets only some light pass through?

56
00:02:18,583 --> 00:02:21,473
Clear glass, frosted glass, or a wooden door?

57
00:02:21,763 --> 00:02:23,073
Show me your fingers!

58
00:02:26,544 --> 00:02:27,524
Locked in!

59
00:02:27,652 --> 00:02:28,522
Three.

60
00:02:28,722 --> 00:02:31,142
Light comes in under my bedroom door.

61
00:02:31,188 --> 00:02:31,928
Two!

62
00:02:32,028 --> 00:02:34,758
Pip, that light goes under your door, not through it!

63
00:02:34,813 --> 00:02:35,443
Two!

64
00:02:35,603 --> 00:02:37,603
Our bathroom window glows at night!

65
00:02:38,555 --> 00:02:39,705
Look closer.

66
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:41,975
The frosted glass.

67
00:02:42,575 --> 00:02:43,545
Torch on.

68
00:02:44,051 --> 00:02:45,371
The light goes in.

69
00:02:46,051 --> 00:02:48,681
On the card: only a soft, dim glow.

70
00:02:49,692 --> 00:02:52,312
Beside the clear glass, it is much dimmer.

71
00:02:52,882 --> 00:02:54,822
Only some of the light passed through.

72
00:02:57,936 --> 00:02:59,126
And the robot?

73
00:02:59,706 --> 00:03:00,846
A blurry shape.

74
00:03:01,456 --> 00:03:03,116
We cannot see it clearly.

75
00:03:06,389 --> 00:03:07,699
The answer is two.

76
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,259
Frosted glass!

77
00:03:09,315 --> 00:03:10,035
Oh!

78
00:03:10,345 --> 00:03:11,705
Only some light.

79
00:03:11,925 --> 00:03:13,565
And a blurry robot!

80
00:03:13,611 --> 00:03:14,641
Two fingers?

81
00:03:14,911 --> 00:03:16,131
One finger up!

82
00:03:16,629 --> 00:03:17,779
Say it with me!

83
00:03:18,493 --> 00:03:21,613
Some materials allow only some light to pass through them.

84
00:03:22,313 --> 00:03:24,203
These materials are translucent.

85
00:03:27,802 --> 00:03:32,122
You cannot clearly see the objects placed behind translucent materials.

86
00:03:32,859 --> 00:03:33,839
Be the light!

87
00:03:34,109 --> 00:03:35,099
Shrink down.

88
00:03:35,379 --> 00:03:36,309
Quietly.

89
00:03:38,597 --> 00:03:40,737
You are light, inside a torch.

90
00:03:41,567 --> 00:03:42,317
Click!

91
00:03:43,137 --> 00:03:44,227
Out you fly.

92
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:46,221
Clear glass ahead.

93
00:03:46,991 --> 00:03:48,461
You pass straight through.

94
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,750
You land on the card: a bright spot!

95
00:03:52,475 --> 00:03:53,325
Again!

96
00:03:54,145 --> 00:03:55,795
Now, frosted glass.

97
00:03:56,469 --> 00:03:58,069
Only some of you pass through.

98
00:03:58,869 --> 00:04:00,069
A soft glow.

99
00:04:02,349 --> 00:04:03,819
Show me your score hand!

100
00:04:04,099 --> 00:04:05,149
More than one?

101
00:04:05,449 --> 00:04:06,809
You beat the Buddies.

102
00:04:07,089 --> 00:04:08,119
Two fingers?

103
00:04:08,389 --> 00:04:09,399
High five!

104
00:04:10,052 --> 00:04:11,742
Did you spot the goldfish?

105
00:04:12,022 --> 00:04:14,252
It was in the glass tank, on the shelf!

106
00:04:14,522 --> 00:04:15,822
Tell someone at home.

107
00:04:16,549 --> 00:04:18,749
Let's read today's key words together!

108
00:04:19,039 --> 00:04:19,799
Ready?

109
00:04:20,086 --> 00:04:21,146
Transparent.

110
00:04:22,699 --> 00:04:23,989
Frosted glass.

111
00:04:25,656 --> 00:04:26,776
Translucent.

112
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,340
Well done!

113
00:04:31,237 --> 00:04:33,727
My robot is hiding behind the door now!

114
00:04:33,781 --> 00:04:35,771
A wooden door, painted white.

115
00:04:36,051 --> 00:04:36,981
Torch on!

116
00:04:37,271 --> 00:04:38,981
How much light will pass through?

117
00:04:39,251 --> 00:04:40,631
Most, some, or none?

118
00:04:40,679 --> 00:04:42,269
Find out in Part Two!

119
00:04:43,629 --> 00:04:44,730
Say it with us!

120
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:46,280
Ready?

121
00:04:46,404 --> 00:04:47,064
One!

122
00:04:47,404 --> 00:04:48,104
two!

123
00:04:48,409 --> 00:04:49,584
Now you know!
